  "@type": "Capability",
  "critical": true,
  "description": "Sealed pressure vessel for conducting chemical reactions under controlled temperature, pressure, agitation, and residence time. Three principal designs: batch stirred-tank (versatile, most common, 50-10,000 L), continuous stirred-tank CSTR (steady-state, large single-product streams), and plug flow PFR (tubular, no back-mixing, highest conversion per unit volume). Performance governed by reaction kinetics, thermodynamics, and heat transfer through the jacket (U 200-500 W/m2-K). Wall thickness per ASME Section VIII: t = (P x R) / (S x E - 0.6 x P). The fundamental unit of chemical manufacturing; every batch reaction, fermentation, acid digestion, and synthesis requires one.",
  "early_win": false,
